# Ravenous Amulet {4}, {T}, Sacrifice this artifact: "Each opponent loses life equal to the number of soul counters on this
# artifact." With no soul counter the number is zero, so Bot2 keeps all 20 life (a sacrifice that still happens: the cost was
# paid). The ability costs exactly {4}: with only three Moxen on the battlefield (Sapphire and Emerald are still in hand) it is refused (`Mana: short`); a fourth is then
# cast and tapped and the activation takes all four and nothing else, leaving Mox Emerald untapped. Bot1's life is unchanged too.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Mox Emerald
Ravenous Amulet
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Ravenous Amulet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
! Bot1.Battlefield.Ravenous Amulet.Activate(Ability: Each opponent loses; Mana: short)
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Ravenous Amulet.Activate(Ability: Each opponent loses)
? Bot1.Mana =
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot1.Graveyard = Ravenous Amulet
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Tapped = false
